# LF in the working tree, on every platform.
#
# This is not a style preference. Git here is configured `core.autocrlf=true`, so a Windows
# checkout used to turn every LF-committed file into CRLF — and Godot renders the carriage
# return inside a `.tscn`'s embedded multi-line string as its own line break. Menu.tscn's
# "How to Play" body is 21 lines that became 42, growing the panel past the bottom of the
# screen with its Back button off it, i.e. the player was trapped in the panel. CI builds
# from a fresh Linux checkout and never saw it, which is why it sat unnoticed.
#
# The blobs were already LF, so this file changes no content — only what lands on disk.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Never touched, whatever they contain.
*.png binary
*.mp3 binary
*.ttf binary
*.otf binary
*.wav binary
*.ogg binary
